operty in the ontology for external follow-up links.\n+- I kept the change minimal and localized rather than rewriting textual definitions without a clearer in-file pattern for dataset-location wording.\n+\n+Background research and review performed:\n+- Read `__issue_context__.json` for the imported issue title, body, and comments.\n+- Checked the target term stanzas in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+- Reviewed the referenced CAP dataset page to confirm it is the human retina bipolar-cell reference dataset.\n+- Reviewed the referenced CellMark PR to understand the NS-Forest-marker request.\n+\n+Scope decision:\n+- The NS-Forest marker part mentioned in the issue appears to refer to upstream CellMark work that was already completed there.\n+- Per repository guidance for this checkout, I edited only `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` and did not attempt unrelated marker-file changes outside the local CL ontology task.\n+\n+Validation performed:\n+- Ran `robot convert --input src/ontology/cl-edit.owl --output /tmp/opencode/cl-edit.ofn` to confirm the edited ontology file parses successfully.\n+\n+Checklist completed:\n+- [x] Read imported issue context\n+- [x] Verified the 13 requested CL terms in `cl-edit.owl`\n+- [x] Confirmed the external dataset target\n+- [x] Added the dataset annotations to all requested classes\n+- [x] Validated ontology syntax with `robot convert`\n+- [x] Committed only the ontology file change\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Added the Cell Annotation Platform reference transcriptomic dataset link (`https://celltype.info/project/544/dataset/1157`) to the 13 